+# Assumptions schedule — Act 25 §4 Acceptance Act
+
+**Bill:** `act25-s4-acceptance-act`. **Sponsor:** `c1a00001` (Clerk).
+**Review date:** 2026-11-22.
+
+| # | Load-bearing claim | Observable evidence that would falsify it |
+|---|---|---|
+| A1 | Act 25's codification content is correct at the exact landed tree | Any of the three cited independent measurements shown not to have examined tree `8ae61f3c…`, or a later finding of a content error in `LAWS.md`'s Act 25 section |
+| A2 | §4's defect is sequencing only, not substance | Evidence that the verification was in fact recorded before the landing |
+| A3 | A recorded House acceptance is a sufficient cure, and this Act is not merely a waiver in disguise | A later implementation skipping pre-landing verification and citing this Act (falsifier F1 in the bill) |
+| A4 | One instance does not erode the rule | Any post-Act bill or implementation with the same defect being treated as covered by this Act |
+
+## Why the assumptions are testable
+
+Each row names a checkable artifact: a Git tree, a measurement record, or a
+subsequent bill. None depends on the sponsor's intent.
